            'authority_url' => 'http://www.evisacam.cm/',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>There is no evidence of a distinct "Sports Visa" product for Cameroon. Indian athletes, coaches, officials and team support staff travelling for a competition or training camp use the standard Cameroon e-Visa or embassy-issued visitor visa.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Supporting Event Documentation</h4><p>Some sports federations hosting events in Cameroon have, in past editions, asked travelling athletes to obtain a support/invitation letter from their national federation to accompany the visa application. This practice has been observed at specific events and is not confirmed as a universal statutory requirement for all sporting travel to Cameroon.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Paid/Professional Engagements</h4><p>No separate work-permit or professional-athlete route for Cameroon was identified in this research. Anyone travelling for a paid or contracted sporting engagement (as opposed to amateur competition) should confirm directly with the Embassy of Cameroon whether any additional authorisation beyond the standard visa is required, since entry permission and permission to be paid are not necessarily the same thing.</p>',
