            'authority_url' => 'https://serviciomigraciones.cl/en/permanencia-transitoria-permit/subcategories/tourists',
            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Chile\'s migration service explicitly lists athletes under the "Permanencia Transitoria" subcategory covering tourist, sporting, business and similar short-term purposes — there is no separate sports-visa product. This covers competitive participation, training visits and similar non-remunerated sporting activity.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Important: No Paid Activity Permitted</h4><p>The official source states that Permanencia Transitoria holders are NOT allowed to carry out any paid activity in Chile. This is a clear and important distinction for Indian athletes: the permit allows entry and participation, but not remuneration, appearance fees, or prize money arrangements that would constitute paid work — those situations should be checked separately with the Servicio Nacional de Migraciones.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Visa Requirement for Indian Nationals</h4><p>Indian passport holders are among the nationalities that may need a prior Chilean consular visa (marked "Sí" on Chile\'s VISTUR/visa-requirement list), unless they qualify for the 2019 exemption for holders of a valid US visa (excluding C/transit) or US green card with 6+ months remaining validity.</p>',
