            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Colombia\'s Cancillería issues guidance to organisers of international events describing a Visa V (Visitante) "Evento" route for participants who require a visa to attend or compete in an event held in Colombia. No separate category specifically naming "athletes," "sport," or "sports competitions" was located in the official material found, so this route is presented as the most relevant evidenced option rather than a confirmed sports-specific product.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Visa-Exempt Nationalities</h4><p>Colombia reportedly exempts visitors from roughly 102 nationalities from the Visa V requirement for stays under 90 days. Whether Indian passport holders are included in that exempt list was NOT confirmed either way in this research — some older, unofficial sources suggest Indian nationals holding a valid US or Schengen visa may be exempt, but this could not be verified against a current official Cancillería source.</p><h4 style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;">Legal Basis</h4><p>Colombia\'s visitor-visa framework is currently set out in Resolución 5477 de 2022 (which replaced the earlier Resolución 6045 de 2017), with Resolución 12509 de 2024 adding a further visitor sub-category. Neither resolution\'s text was reviewed in full during this research to confirm sport-specific wording.</p>',
